<title>NEW ZEALAND: Simpson named RBNZ non-executive director.</title>
<headline>Simpson named RBNZ non-executive director.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Treasurer Winston Peters said on Monday businessman Gil Simpson was apppinted a non-executive director of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand.</p>
<p>In a statement the Treasury said Simpson brought wide experience to his new position. Non-executives have no input into policies and management at the bank, however.</p>
<p>The chief executive of Christchurch-based computer company Aoraki Corporation, Simpson is due to serve a five year term on the board.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
</text>
